WEBVTT

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.690
Well, Nii-san, how do I look?

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.410
<b>A Place One Wants to Be Forever</b>

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.000
It's cold.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.420
The cherry blossoms may be in bloom,

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.510
but I guess spring's still far off.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.580
Himeno sure is late today.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.770
I wonder if she caught a cold.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.420
Himeno, I'm coming in.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.530
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh—

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.040
Why?!

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.560
N-No, those pink panties 
weren't coming out,

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.130
so I started thinking you 
might be over-Himenoing,

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:31.280
or that you might be bedridden 
with a cold bra or...

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:43.130
I-I see you're maturing 
as a woman, too, Himeno.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.450
Onii-san's very proud of you! Yes!

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:54.510
So, is that all you have to say?

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.120
Now, how long are you 
planning to ogle me?

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:01.190
No, I mean...

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.970
I wasn't trying to peek!

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.020
Just hurry up and get out!

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.130
I-I'm sorry!

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.470
I-I got a real good look...

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.500
I should probably go on ahead...

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.930
Receiving Mail...

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.970
<i>Make sure you wait for me, okay?</i>

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:28.400
<i>I have a lot to talk to you about.</i>

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.730
<i>If you go on ahead of me,</i>

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.990
<i>I'll kill you, Nii-san!</i>

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.610
Good grief. Nii-san, you horny perv.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:53.340
You have no delicacy.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:54.840
I said I'm sorry.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:59.010
Y-You're not allowed to remember 
what you just saw, either, got it?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.850
Please forget about it quickly!

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.940
W-Well... It is true that 
I was about to be late,

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.110
so I'll overlook it this time.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:16.330
Thanks.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.470
S-Speaking of which, 
the bus is a lot more crowded

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.230
when we miss our usual one, isn't it?

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.300
It's unusual for you to oversleep.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.070
Did you pull an all-nighter last night?

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.340
No, that isn't the case,

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.270
but it seems I turned my 
alarm off in my sleep.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.990
Are your manners okay?

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.010
Well, I guess everyone has those days.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.120
Are you all right, Himeno?

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:45.620
Y-Yes,

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.060
I'm fine.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.470
We apologize for the inconvenience.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:57.120
A pedestrian jumped into the street, 
so we made a sudden stop.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.520
Resuming now.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.140
U-Um... Nii-san?

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.960
I'm fine now, so...

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:09.440
Oh! Sorry!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.080
No, um, thank you.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.170
Mathematics
N Test

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:54.710
Nii-san!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:55.790
Excuse me, Katsuragi-san?

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.060
Oh, yes? What is it?

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.960
Katsuragi-san, if you'd like,

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:02.170
would you join us for karaoke after school?

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.100
We've found a cheap place!

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.640
I'm sorry, I have club 
activities after class.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.970
Oh well, then.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.720
Katsuragi-san's popular with 
the girls too, isn't she?

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.780
Maybe I should give a shot 
at asking her out, too?

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:22.060
<i>The #1 "girl I want to make 
into my bride," huh?</i>

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.780
Hey, Kiyotaka, let's hit the cafeteria.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.830
Oh, sure.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.640
Well, why don't we all 
have lunch together, then?

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:31.960
Huh? Um...

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.710
Let's hurry up and eat.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.980
So, spill the beans. How is it?

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:49.750
Well, it's the same udon 
they always serve...

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.210
Not the udon!

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:52.820
Progress between you and Himeno!

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:57.010
Huh? What's this about 
Himeno all of a sudden?

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:58.580
Don't play dumb with me.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.060
You were just staring at her.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.920
I wasn't really...

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.930
I want to hear this, too.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:06.500
Nakayama?

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.600
Mind if I sit next to you?

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:11.520
I don't mind, but...

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.340
Then pardon me.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.940
You're not with Himeno-chan 
and the others today?

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:18.790
I overslept this morning 
and didn't have time

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:21.000
to make lunch, so I 
had to eat here alone.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:25.150
More importantly, Kiyotaka-kun, 
what do you think of Himeno?

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:26.830
What do I think?

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:29.120
I think she's my childhood friend.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.820
That's not it!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:34.030
We're asking if you want to 
do <i>this</i> and <i>that</i> to her!

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:36.410
I wasn't going that far...

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.600
But... Do you?

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:40.630
I don't think about—

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:41.800
How filthy!

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:43.850
Huh?

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.640
Newspaper Club

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.540
Now then, I'd like to begin today's meeting.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:54.250
I guess we'll start with our 
reports from yesterday, then?

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:57.110
To summarize our 
investigation of old articles,

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:59.640
during the two periods in which the 
Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree has bloomed,

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.620
there were several reports of 
strange people and phenomena.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.760
What do you mean by "strange people"?

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:10.100
Well, a girl who can read minds,

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.730
or a girl with perfect 
memory, and so forth.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.300
That's our Ricca-san!

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.370
You came up with that setting on spot!

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:18.400
How sad...

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.400
Hey, you underclassman!

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.110
This is what was 
written in the articles,

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:23.980
and it has nothing to 
do with my past life.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:27.080
Sorry, my tongue slipped.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.010
How cute, Ricca-san!

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:31.920
Whatever.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:34.850
So, how did it go on 
your end, Taka-kun?

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:37.600
Um, well, it seems there were several

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.610
accidents and incidents with unknown causes

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.600
occurring in the months before 
the Cherry Blossom wilted.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.150
Accidents with unknown causes?

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:45.960
Yeah.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.970
Such occurrences kept increasing,

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:51.300
most drastically so in the 
month before it wilted.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:54.970
Then, once it wilted, the accidents 
and incidents suddenly decreased.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:56.910
We'll need to create more

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:59.780
detailed statistics for these incidents, then.

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:02.160
How did the interviews go?

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:06.660
Um, it appears that our 
former principal knew a lot

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.600
about the Everlasting Cherry 
 Blossom Tree and mysterious powers.

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:13.040
She disappeared when the Cherry 
Blossom wilted the first time,

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:15.370
and they say she suddenly came back

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.630
to Hatsune Island about twenty years ago.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.570
Our former principal?

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.460
What was her name?

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.540
It's an incredible coincidence, but...

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.700
It was Yoshino Sakura-san.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.070
Yoshino...

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:30.540
Sakura?

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.710
Yes. And with the same 
kanji as your names.

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:35.910
Maybe you're related?

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.350
No, I've never heard of her.
 You, Lulu-nee?

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:41.190
I don't know her, either.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:43.690
Sakura, Sakura...

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:45.890
Something about that bugs me.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:50.060
This is the former principal, 
Yoshino Sakura-san.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.060
Greetings from your Principal

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.060
Yoshino Sakura

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.930
Sakura...?

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:01.480
Sakura Shopping District

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.760
<i>Sakura? That Sakura?</i>

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:12.350
<i>No, if she was our former principal,</i>

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.790
<i>then there's no way she's that young.</i>

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:15.950
Nii-san.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:19.700
Hey, Nii-san!

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:22.290
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.560
Sheesh!

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:24.960
So, what is it?

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:26.860
Oh... Um...

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.170
I just thought it's been a while.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:33.840
What has?

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:36.460
Y-You know...

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:39.010
Th-The two of us being alone together.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:41.670
We go to school together 
every morning, don't we?

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:43.370
Th-That's not what I mean!

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:44.710
You know...

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:50.500
Lately, we haven't had much 
quiet time together.

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:54.030
Now that you mention it, that's true.

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:56.490
So...

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:58.500
Well...

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.240
Um...

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:03.290
I mean... We used to...

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.000
What's up with you?

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:09.870
No, i-i-it's nothing.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:17.880
Well, Ricca-san has been 
awfully fired up lately.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.090
N-Nii-san...

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.490
I don't care about you anymore, Nii-san!

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:27.060
Do what you want!

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:29.320
Hmph!

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:32.740
Why is Himeno mad at me?

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.490
Sakura?

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.780
Onii-chan!

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.370
Third Kazami Park

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:05.690
It's done!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.690
Tada!

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.040
Incredible.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.290
Incredible, isn't it?

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.260
Onii-chan?

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.610
Oh, sorry, sorry!

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:12.660
Onii-chan, you looked very sad.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:16.010
I wasn't.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:19.600
Onii-chan, good boy, good boy!

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:22.510
I'm here for you, so there's 
nothing to be sad about.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.180
Thanks, Sakura.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:30.990
All right then, Sakura, 
gather lots of sand.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:33.050
Onii-chan, are you going 
to make something?

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.950
Yeah. I'm going to make 
something incredible.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.510
What's that?

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:39.900
You'll find out when it's done.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.120
Yay, I can't wait!

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.590
All right, Utamaru, let's gather sand!

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:51.140
Hey, Sakura?

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:54.340
Do you know Yoshino?

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.210
Yoshino?

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.140
No, it's fine if you don't know.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:01.800
All right, let's make something incredible.

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.410
Yeah! I can't wait!

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.930
Lulu-nee, the bath's ready.

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.910
Okay, thanks, Taka-kun.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:31.710
Himeno?

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:35.340
Are you awake, Nii-san?
I'm waiting outside.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:51.060
Hey, Nii-san.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:53.400
What's up, texting this late?

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:56.770
Well... I-I thought it's been a while

00:15:56.770 --> 00:15:59.870
since we spent some quiet 
time together, so...

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.140
Am I bothering you?

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.540
No, not really.

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:10.450
So, um... Want to go for a walk?

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.610
What? Were you feeling 
lonely or something?

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.670
O-Of course I wasn't!

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.300
It's not like that...

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:19.720
A-And what about you, Nii-san? 
Aren't you feeling lonely?

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:26.460
More like, a bit regretful.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.130
Regretful?

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.160
I'm glad that we're all

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:33.070
having more fun together as 
the newspaper club, but...

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:37.440
It's true that you and I have 
had less time together.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:40.980
It's kind of like...

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.960
It feels like a relationship I thought 
would never change

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.990
already has changed a bit...

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:49.250
And I regret it a little.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:52.760
I see.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:57.520
Nii-san, let's hold hands like we used to.

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:01.200
What's wrong with that? 
It's not like anyone's watching.

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.900
It's just... a bit embarrassing.

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.600
I-It's embarrassing for me, 
too, so we're even!

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.690
Come on!

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:14.980
This is... kind of nostalgic.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:16.880
Yeah...

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:20.560
Let's walk, Nii-san.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:20.120
Nii-san, the truth is, I...

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:25.500
Nii-san.

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:35.100
Himeno.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:41.060
Just another ten, no...

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:43.770
Five minutes...

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:01.390
Himeno's late again today.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.670
This time I'm knocking.

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:08.570
Himeno! Are you still asleep?

00:19:08.570 --> 00:19:10.230
If you're changing, answer me.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:15.500
Himeno, we're going to be late!

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:27.910
Nii-san... don't look... 
anymore, it's embarrassing...

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.110
Sorry!

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:34.010
Wait, she's sleep talking?!

00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:35.920
Good grief, what timing...

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:40.800
Ah... ngh... no... Nii-san, don't...!

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.530
Jeez. Come on, Himeno, wake up!

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:47.470
Ngh, ah... don't be that rough...!

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:49.690
You won't wake up if I'm not rough.

00:19:49.690 --> 00:19:51.270
Now come on and wake up!

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:56.320
Nii-san, you're really forward today...

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.010
Because we're about to be late.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:00.420
Late?

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:01.190
Yeah.

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.150
Hey. Good morning.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:19.500
It's none of my business, 
but I think you

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:21.830
should do something 
about the way you sleep.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:27.040
J-Just get out of here right now!

00:21:57.560 --> 00:22:00.060
You actually set your alarm clock, right?

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:03.830
Yes, but I guess I turned 
it off in my sleep.

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:06.070
This never happened before.

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:07.440
I see.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:10.010
By the way, what were you 
dreaming about earlier?

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:14.350
Wha— Why do I have to 
tell you that, Nii-san?!

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:17.820
I'm curious since you slept in again.

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:21.640
Besides, I was in your dream, right?

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:23.960
You were saying something 
about "rough" in your sleep?

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:29.270
Th-That has nothing to 
do with you, Nii-san!

00:22:29.270 --> 00:22:32.100
I'll never, never tell you what I 
was dreaming about this morning!

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:35.600
I see, judging by that reaction,

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:37.500
you must've been having an erotic dream?

00:22:37.700 --> 00:22:40.460
Wha— I-I was not!

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:43.470
B-Besides, you're the 
one who came after me!

00:22:45.170 --> 00:22:47.740
So you really had an erotic dream?

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:53.650
What kind of dreams are you having?!

00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:57.590
I-If you come after me like 
that, I can't refuse, can I?!

00:22:57.590 --> 00:22:59.190
Wh-What are you saying, idiot?!

00:22:59.450 --> 00:23:03.530
I-I mean in my dream! 
D-Don't get the wrong idea!

00:23:03.530 --> 00:23:06.390
Of course not! I wouldn't go—

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:09.230
What?! Y-You're saying 
you never would?!

00:23:09.230 --> 00:23:12.670
N-No, that's not what 
I wanted to say, I...

